title: "But do you understand it?"
date: 2026-08-16
---

You watch a youtube video of someone talking about a fairly complex subject matter; one that they have spent considerable time researching and reading about(hopefully). You watch the distillation; you are given the conclusion; and you think you *understand* it?

If you have decent comprehension you are particularly susceptible to this. You listen to a video and the person makes a highly sophisticated argument and it all *makes sense* to you. You are able to parse the arguments in real time and this gives you the feeling of having understood it. You're also able to regurgitate most of it in a fairly convincing manner. But do you understand it?

You get the feeling of understanding something complex without putting in the work to understand it. The mother bird eats the food for you and spits it into your mouth; and you eat it. You confuse *being able to follow a well structured argument* with *understanding the subject matter deeply*, to say nothing of the biases of the distiller that have been baked into your second hand understanding. And you go out into the world and regurgitate it again.

But it doesn't matter, cause no one is putting in the effort now and so you don't get caught. You float through the world without ever deeply understanding what you are saying because no one can catch your bluff, including yourself. Everyone is a copy of a copy of someone else doing the work. Why is it that when I get into it with someone nowadays, I can tell three arguments in what the next fifteen are going to be? 

You're lazy, you like feeling smart without putting in the effort. You regurgitate half understood arguments with passion and pretend to understand it. You're an imposter. 

AI is making all this so much worse. Now you can do tangible work without understanding anything. Now you *don't even have to look at the code.Why think? Claude will do it for you. Why remember anything? Claude will do it for you. Why gain expertise in anything when Claude can do it for you?

You're trading your intelligence for a subscription service that sells it back to you.

Do you understand?
